{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793912120,"nonce":"yvs9DDMTzFLzclW6Z+e8uGEkJrE=","title":"Filter non-heap words before out-of-line marker calls","message":"Follow-up to e0cf9bd. Marker::scan reads every aligned word and excludes only pointers back into the scanned range. It then calls Marker::consider even for zero, ASCII data and words outside the entire managed heap. consider immediately rejects those values using self.lo/self.hi. Frozen NUC assembly confirms consider is out of line in drain_to; the direct caller can reject these values before paying that call.\n\nThe large-block cold-helper experiment did not improve tokenize: 378 normal wall samples yield a paired ratio of 1.01928, and seven diagnostic pairs show mark medians 15.53 -\u003e 17.31 ms despite shrinking consider from 1,192 to 607 bytes. Do not fold that withheld change into this experiment.\n\nAdd the same inclusive-low/exclusive-high heap bounds to the existing scan condition, preserving the word reads, own-range exclusion, interior-pointer acceptance and mark/work ordering. Keep consider's own checks for other callers. Attribution/explain paths remain unchanged. No root-lifetime, heap-growth or GC policy change is needed.\n\nUse isolated source over 6d9f9ba3 with original inliner and collector, existing collector/pool-cursor checks, frozen LLVM-off NUC measurements and collection traces. If promising, apply separately over the landed ordering fix and run full pinned official TS corpus, local conformance and broader frozen controls before committing. Initial bounded experiment covers tokenize, binary_trees and pipeline; raw evidence will live under /private/tmp/zyntax-mark-filter and the matching persistent NUC cache.","files":null}]}